---
/**
 * Brief behind the "AI build-out contagion" row on /risk/. Backstory is dated
 * text. Where we stand and the price levels in What we're watching are built
 * from the row's feeds at build time (src/lib/ai-contagion-brief.ts), so they
 * move with every feed push. The long essay that lived here is in
 * docs/archive/pages/risk/.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import RiskWatch from '../../components/RiskWatch.astro';
import { aiContagionBriefNow } from '../../lib/ai-contagion-brief';
import '../../styles/risk.css';

const title = 'AI build-out contagion';
const subhead = 'A slip in AI campus building can travel to chip stocks and then to the whole market. The numbers below come from the /risk/ watch-list feed.';

const brief = aiContagionBriefNow();

const watchItems = [
  ...brief.watch,
  '23 Nov: New Mexico\'s decision on the Project Jupiter fuel-cell air permit.',
  '1 Feb 2027: the Green Chile pipeline in-service date.',
  'New force majeure or rent-deferral notices on other AI campuses, especially ones tied to power, gas, or permits.',
  'AI campus loans that fail to syndicate, meaning the lead lender cannot sell pieces to other investors, as happened with Blue Owl\'s roughly $4 billion Lancaster, Pennsylvania package earlier in 2026.',
  'Credit rating actions tied to AI spending by hyperscalers, the largest cloud companies.',
];

const sources = [
  { text: 'TechCrunch, Oracle sends force majeure notice on its New Mexico Stargate data center', href: 'https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/24/oracle-sends-force-majeure-notice-on-its-new-mexico-stargate-data-center/' },
  { text: 'El Paso Matters, Oracle could defer Project Jupiter rent payments over power supply delays', href: 'https://elpasomatters.org/2026/09/24/project-jupiter-rent-force-majeure-new-mexico-oracle-ai-el-paso-data-center/' },
  { text: 'Reuters, Oracle, Blue Owl project delay sends ripples through AI financing, sources say', href: 'https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/oracle-blue-owl-project-delay-sends-ripples-through-ai-financing-sources-say-2026-09-24/' },
  { text: 'U.S. Census Bureau, Construction Spending historical data', href: 'https://www.census.gov/construction/c30/historical_data.html' },
  { text: 'Yahoo Finance, SMH price history', href: 'https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/SMH/history/' },
  { text: 'State Street Global Advisors, SPDR S&P 500 ETF Trust (SPY) holdings', href: 'https://www.ssga.com/us/en/intermediary/etfs/spdr-sp-500-etf-trust-spy' },
];
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} - Rycode`}
  description={subhead}
  variant="risk"
>
  <article class="risk-digest risk-brief">
    <header class="risk-digest-head">
      <h1 class="risk-digest-title">{title}</h1>
      <p class="risk-digest-subhead">{subhead}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="risk-digest-main">
      <section class="risk-digest-section" id="backstory">
        <h2>Backstory</h2>
        <p>In late September 2026, Oracle sent a force majeure notice to the developer of Project Jupiter, a Stargate-class AI data-center campus near Santa Teresa, New Mexico. A force majeure clause is a contract term that lets a party excuse or defer obligations when events outside its control get in the way. Reporting says the notice preserves Oracle's right to defer rent for up to three years if the campus misses its online date because of power commitments. Oracle says the project remains on its planned schedule. Blue Owl, whose STACK Infrastructure unit is the developer and holds about $3 billion of equity, says its financial commitments are unchanged.</p>
        <p>The campus is designed around about 2.45 GW (gigawatts, or billions of watts) of on-site Bloom Energy fuel cells, which turn natural gas into electricity. The Green Chile pipeline that would supply the gas has slipped to about 1 Feb 2027 after New Mexico State Land Office route denials. The air-quality permit for the fuel-cell plant has a state decision deadline of 23 Nov.</p>
        <p>Reuters reports the notice chilled AI infrastructure financing talks, including SB Energy's Ohio campus deal, and SB Energy delayed its IPO the same week. S&amp;P Global Ratings had already cut Oracle to its lowest investment-grade rating.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="risk-digest-section" id="where-we-stand">
        <h2>Where we stand</h2>
        <p class="risk-brief-asof">{brief.asOf}</p>
        <p>The row tracks one chain. Build-outs get delayed, then the market reacts to the AI build getting harder, then the broad market drops because it leans so heavily on AI.</p>
        <p><strong>Step 1, Build.</strong> {brief.build}</p>
        <p><strong>Step 2, Chips.</strong> {brief.chips}</p>
        <p><strong>Step 3, Market.</strong> {brief.market}</p>
        <p>{brief.strain}</p>
      </section>

      <section class="risk-digest-section" id="watching">
        <h2>What we're watching</h2>
        <RiskWatch items={watchItems} />
      </section>

      <section class="risk-digest-section risk-digest-sources" id="sources">
        <h2>Sources</h2>
        <ol>
          {sources.map((source) => (
            <li>
              <a href={source.href}>{source.text}</a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .risk-brief .risk-digest-main {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .risk-brief .risk-brief-asof {
    margin-top: -0.35rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--digest-faint, rgba(248, 250, 252, 0.4));
  }
</style>
